<pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.14" change_id="Idf0ded22d6731d97649c3129f70ee5f0b96894f4" commit="20bf2c9c2ee9ce9147c9c6cbbc8e7dde7e3af260" commit_message="CHROMIUM: drm: bridge/dw_hdmi: Init i2c after resume  We need to make sure we are able to do i2c over the HDMI i2c port again after suspend/resume, so we'll put an init in the resume function.  Note that we refactor the initialize_hdmi_ih_mutes() a bit because at resume time it's wise to init the i2c stuff before we init the rest of the interrupts.  The initialize_hdmi_ih_mutes() was always duplicated at bind time anyway...  BUG=chrome-os-partner:34741 TEST=HDMI vs. suspend/resume, broken monitor, HDCP, etc.  Change-Id: Idf0ded22d6731d97649c3129f70ee5f0b96894f4 Signed-off-by: Douglas Anderson &lt;dianders@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/302800 Commit-Ready: Yakir Yang &lt;ykk@rock-chips.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Yakir Yang &lt;ykk@rock-chips.com&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="302800" owner_email="dianders@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/00/302800/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.14" change_id="Iff678fb49828db9b8026422e302a03f687a7c862" commit="2ec18fda138d46e0f58c8529a1e729daa28a199a" commit_message="CHROMIUM: drm: bridge/dw_hdmi: fix i2cm standard mode setting error  I have uploaded a patch to switch DDC to standard mode in (https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/298270), but that change have influence the &quot;spare register&quot; in I2CM_DIV, I know this haven't cause some know bug, but we need to fix it.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:34741 TEST=None  Change-Id: Iff678fb49828db9b8026422e302a03f687a7c862 Signed-off-by: Yakir Yang &lt;ykk@rock-chips.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/302751 Commit-Ready: Douglas Anderson &lt;dianders@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Douglas Anderson &lt;dianders@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Douglas Anderson &lt;dianders@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="302751" owner_email="ykk@rock-chips.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="3" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/51/302751/3" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.14" change_id="I59991111dd781483b9b27f7e96bd6854cd631aa5" commit="eb1172b49c31a7176e65d51b3d5d51c3233c08cd" commit_message="CHROMIUM: drm: bridge/dw_hdmi: add HDCP support  dw_hdmi will provide an &quot;hdcp_key&quot; debug node in sysfs, userspace can pass the right HDCP KEY to driver through this node. As for now there are an HDCP service in rootfs that will read the vpd space to find the right HDCP KEY, and then pass those context to the &quot;hdcp_key&quot; node, so driver can start the hdcp function successfully.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:34741 TEST=FIRST YOU SHOULD DO THOSE STEP:         1. Cherry-pick https://chrome-internal-review.googlesource.com/#/c/227461/,            make sure &quot;/sbin/hdcp_pass_key.sh&quot; &quot;/lib/udev/rules.d/99-veyron-hdmi.rules&quot; exist.         2. Buy this video &quot;https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=XfRY0ASZHuU&quot;      WITH HDCP KEY SITUATION:         1. flash encrypt key to vpd area, and reboot chromebook.           $ vpd -O; vpd -s hdcp_key_v1_4=balabalabala...; dump_vpd_log --force;         2. Go to test video in youtube and see high rez options if            not in developer mode.         3. In developer mode, run &quot;modetest&quot; and see that HDCP is            enabled while playing &quot;requested&quot; HDCP content.      WITH WRONG HDCP KEY SITUATION:         1. flash encrypt hack key to vpd area, and reboot chromebook.           $ vpd -O; vpd -s hdcp_key=balabalahackhack...; dump_vpd_log --force;         2. You won't be given high resolution options, but you'll get            spam in the logs.      WITHOUT HDCP KEY SITUATION:         1. Erase the vpd area, and reboot chromebook.           $ vpd -O; dump_vpd_log --force;         2. You won't be given high resolution options.      SUSPEND/RESUME WITH WRONG/RIGHT HDCP ENABLE:         - Try all above after suspend/resume  Change-Id: I59991111dd781483b9b27f7e96bd6854cd631aa5 Signed-off-by: Yakir Yang &lt;ykk@rock-chips.com&gt; Signed-off-by: Douglas Anderson &lt;dianders@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/237585 " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="237585" owner_email="ykk@rock-chips.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="53" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/85/237585/53" remote="cros" total_fail_count="4"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.14" change_id="I3cbd17b0f091098df9cba401a7ccb126191f1c39" commit="6e5a7cae86cddb84036460ff2a7e650144963746" commit_message="CHROMIUM: ARM: dts: rockchip: add efuse node to hdmi device  Quote the efuse node to hdmi device, so dw_hdmi driver could call the rockchip_efuse_get_uid function to read the cpu uid.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:44922 TEST=dw_hdmi driver could read cpu uid success.  Change-Id: I3cbd17b0f091098df9cba401a7ccb126191f1c39 Signed-off-by: Yakir Yang &lt;ykk@rock-chips.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/300372 Commit-Ready: Douglas Anderson &lt;dianders@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Douglas Anderson &lt;dianders@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Douglas Anderson &lt;dianders@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="300372" owner_email="ykk@rock-chips.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="26" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/72/300372/26" remote="cros" total_fail_count="5"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I94249ce5bfe52f99b0af399298aac917112e72dc" commit="cdf0a1b065